# Ignored modernization suggestions
# Format: <date> <category> <description>
2026-08-17 crypto-elliptic-to-ecdh Not migratable: internal/cert/cert.go and internal/acme/acme.go use crypto/elliptic.P256/P384/P521 to feed ecdsa.GenerateKey and x509 cert/CSR signing. crypto/ecdh only supports ECDH key agreement, not ECDSA signing, so there is no replacement here.
2026-08-17 sync-oncevalue-hostname-asn Skipped for internal/api/hostname.go hostCache() and internal/api/asn.go asnCache(): Handler has no constructor and is built via bare struct literals across 11+ call sites including tests, so the zero-value-safe sync.Once + field pattern is correct; sync.OnceValue would need every call site to initialize a func() field.
2026-08-17 shardutil-l1-cache Skipped unifying internal/cache/l1.go's shard(h uint64) into internal/shardutil.FNV1a: it hashes an already-computed uint64, not a string key, so it doesn't fit the shared helper's signature. ratelimit.go, nxguard.go, connlimit.go, and loginguard.go were unified; l1.go was left as-is.
2026-08-17 golangci-lint-tool-directive Reverted: adding golangci-lint as a go.mod `tool` directive pulls in its entire linter-plugin dependency tree (~150 linters), tripling go.mod and adding ~450 lines to go.sum, for no benefit since CI already installs golangci-lint independently via the pinned golangci-lint-action. Kept a version-pinned `go run .../golangci-lint@v2.12.2` in the Makefile instead. govulncheck's tool directive was kept (cheap: ~9 lines).
2026-08-25 t-parallel-adoption Applied across ~40 packages (acme, api, cache, cert, config, dhcp, filter, firewall, geoip, installer, querylog, recursive, tuning, tunnel, update, upstream — ~330 t.Parallel() calls total), auditing every test file for shared/global state first. Left non-parallel: tests that mutate a package-level var used for HTTP/mock injection (e.g. internal/api's siteFetchClient, ripestatNetworkInfo, axfrPort, crtShBase, fastestResolvers; internal/update's supportsGOAMD64V3; internal/recursive's SetDefaultRootHints/SetDefaultServerTimeout) — safe because Go runs every non-parallel test to completion before any parallel group starts, so these run in full isolation; tests calling t.Setenv or raw os.Setenv (t.Setenv panics under a parallel ancestor; raw os.Setenv in internal/installer/e2e_test.go races real process env); internal/tuning/cgroup_linux_test.go and sysctl_linux_test.go (every test there mutates shared package-level fixture-path vars); a real-socket-binding DHCP test gated behind an opt-in env var.
2026-08-25 t-parallel-dnsserver-reverted Not applied to internal/dnsserver (14 files, ~93 candidate call sites) despite passing the same per-file audit: the package's dns.Msg/[]byte pools (reqPool in udp_server.go, packBufPool in packpool.go) are process-wide sync.Pools shared by every *Handler instance, not per-test-isolated. `go test -race` alone didn't catch it (synchronized pool access, not a data race) — only a real stress run (`go test -count=3 -parallel=32`) surfaced actual cross-test corruption: TestPackBufPoolGrows failing its own retention check, TestDoH3RoundTrip unpacking a corrupted response, TestHandlerCoalescesConcurrentIdenticalQueries getting another test's message ID. Revisit only with a from-scratch pool-awareness audit (which tests exercise ServeDNS/serve() and thus touch the shared pools), not a blanket sweep.
